    LLM: 'Game: Carpet. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Carpet is a simple and rewarding patience (solitaire) game. Four Aces form the foundations, twenty cards are laid out in a 5Ã—4 grid called the 'carpet,' and the remaining cards form a stock. The goal is to build all cards onto the foundations in suit from Ace to King.",
    objective: 'Move all cards onto the four foundations, building each up in suit from Ace to King.',
    gameplay: 'Foundations build up in suit (Aceâ†’2â†’3â†’...â†’King). Cards available for play: all cards in the carpet, and the top card of the discard pile. Empty spaces in the carpet may be filled from the discard pile. Deal from stock one card at a time onto discard pile at any time. No redeals - when stock is empty, dealing stops.',
